{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017fVWFFjhi5er15KgHkFZKK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: neurico-paper-writer-pitfalls\n3\tdescription: \"NeuriCo paper-writing runs: neurips_2025 [final] and general.tex compile traps, and REPORT.md references/counts need checking\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: acab57a5-067a-4a1b-b5bb-257976113aa0\n8\t  modified: 2026-10-31T06:20:31.127Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tTraps in the NeuriCo paper-writing stage (seen 2026-10-30, embedding_collapse_repetition run):\n12\t- `\\usepackage[final]{neurips_2025}` sets no track, so `\\@trackname` is undefined at `\\maketitle`. Keep the mandated line and add `\\makeatletter\\providecommand{\\@trackname}{}\\makeatother` after it.\n13\t- `commands/general.tex` renews `\\algorithmicindent`, so load `algpseudocode` before `\\input{commands/general}`.\n14\t- `paper_examples/` may hold only a README; style then comes from `templates/paper_writing/`.\n15\t- REPORT.md references \"from memory\" can be wrong (venues, years, author names), and summary counts can count ties or significance as strict wins. Check citations online and recompute counts from `results/*.csv`.\n16\t- Also seen 2026-10-31 (fp_error_propagation run): REPORT.md summary ranges can be off in small ways, and a blanket claim (\"largest source\") can hide one exception or quote one format's correlation. Recompute from `results/`, including `*.partial_*.jsonl`, which may hold arms missing from the final jsonl. Report author lists can't be taken from two-column pdftotext order; use the arXiv page.\n17\t- `/tmp/<fixed-name>` may be unwritable on this host; pipe scripts through `python - <<'E'` or use `mktemp -d`.\n18\t\n19\t**Why:** each cost a debugging step, and the wrong citations would have reached the paper.\n20\t**How to apply:** do these checks before drafting. See also [[neurico-host-local-llm-fallback]].\n21\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f205d79e-9dcc-4336-8ac8-c0edce33ebd6","uuid":"1c3aa581-9555-481b-98a4-beaa9942a941","timestamp":"2026-10-31T06:53:52.502Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/summereunann/.claude/projects/-data/memory/neurico-paper-writer-pitfalls.md","content":"---\nname: neurico-paper-writer-pitfalls\ndescription: \"NeuriCo paper-writing runs: neurips_2025 [final] and general.tex compile traps, and REPORT.md references/counts need checking\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: acab57a5-067a-4a1b-b5bb-257976113aa0\n  modified: 2026-10-31T06:20:31.127Z\n---\n\nTraps in the NeuriCo paper-writing stage (seen 2026-10-30, embedding_collapse_repetition run):\n- `\\usepackage[final]{neurips_2025}` sets no track, so `\\@trackname` is undefined at `\\maketitle`. Keep the mandated line and add `\\makeatletter\\providecommand{\\@trackname}{}\\makeatother` after it.\n- `commands/general.tex` renews `\\algorithmicindent`, so load `algpseudocode` before `\\input{commands/general}`.\n- `paper_examples/` may hold only a README; style then comes from `templates/paper_writing/`.\n- REPORT.md references \"from memory\" can be wrong (venues, years, author names), and summary counts can count ties or significance as strict wins. Check citations online and recompute counts from `results/*.csv`.\n- Also seen 2026-10-31 (fp_error_propagation run): REPORT.md summary ranges can be off in small ways, and a blanket claim (\"largest source\") can hide one exception or quote one format's correlation. Recompute from `results/`, including `*.partial_*.jsonl`, which may hold arms missing from the final jsonl. Report author lists can't be taken from two-column pdftotext order; use the arXiv page.\n- `/tmp/<fixed-name>` may be unwritable on this host; pipe scripts through `python - <<'E'` or use `mktemp -d`.\n\n**Why:** each cost a debugging step, and the wrong citations would have reached the paper.\n**How to apply:** do these checks before drafting. See also [[neurico-host-local-llm-fallback]].\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017fVWFFjhi5er15KgHkFZKK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
