{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qbv3rXWKP9c5WoaPMcqYmt","type":"tool_result","content":"4:At geometrically spaced checks every live replica is quenched to see which minimum it falls into.\n5:Basin exit is decided by a converged quench. Loss and distance trajectories are saved, so loss-level and\\nradius first-passage definitions can be applied post hoc.\n12:GATE = 0.3     # distance after the gate quench above which the long quench is run\n13:R_OUT = 0.05   # distance after the long quench above which the replica may have left the basin\n14:BAR_MIN, DL_MIN = 1e-5, 2e-5   # an exit also needs a segment barrier or a change of minimum loss\n47:    loss, dist, gate = nanarr(), nanarr(), nanarr()\n53:    # Gate from a pilot on two minima: after q_gate quench steps, in-basin replicas sit <0.04 from th* and escaped\n54:    # ones >2.5. Replicas past GATE get the long quench, whose converged end point decides.\n56:    q_lr, q_gate, q_long = 1.0 / lmax, int(qm * 1500 * max(1, lmax)), int(qm * 5000 * max(1, lmax))\n69:        Q = ns.quench(net, x, q_lr, q_gate)\n71:        gate[ids, c] = dq.cpu().numpy()\n72:        cand = dq > GATE\n75:            Ql = ns.quench(net, Q[cand], q_lr, q_long - q_gate)\n78:            # points have no barrier AND no loss change; a real neighbour always shows at least one of them.\n83:                bq[out] = ns.segment_barrier(net, Ql[out], th_star)\n100:    return dict(grid=np.array(grid), loss=loss, dist=dist, gate=gate, t_exit=t_exit, d_exit=d_exit, l_exit=l_exit,\n179:def quench(net, th, lr, steps, beta=0.9):\n180:    \"\"\"Full-batch heavy-ball descent; stiff directions relax so the point falls into its own basin.\"\"\"\n185:        m = beta * m + g\n203:def classify(net, x, th_star, Hinv, lmax, q0=150, chord=25, q_long=5000, r_in=0.02, r_out=0.05):\nfig1_e0_validation.png\nfig2_distributions.png\nfig3_hazard.png\nfig4_adam_sgd.png\nfig5_batch_scaling.png\nfig6_saddles.png","is_error":false}]},"pa