{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZtKsLZda3gqum2f5ag5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The paper is finished: `paper_draft/main.pdf` is 12 pages and compiles from a clean rebuild with no errors, overfull boxes or undefined citations. The title is \"Escape Times from Neural Network Basins: Delay and Heterogeneity, Not a Weibull Shape Law\", and the author line is `NeuriCo`. I rendered every page to check the layout, and went through the language, formatting and structure checklist.\n\n**The paper differs from `REPORT.md` in some places.** I recomputed the numbers from `results/`, and some of the report's claims didn't hold up. I left `REPORT.md` unchanged, so it now disagrees with the paper on these points:\n\n| Topic | `REPORT.md` | Paper |\n|---|---|---|\n| **η/B law on digits** | \"Only partly\" supported, ratios 0.55 and 1.28 | **Inconclusive.** All three (0.05, 8) medians hit the 150,000-step cap, so 0.55 mostly reflects the cap. Only one minimum has both medians observed for the other ratio, and it gives 1.03. |\n| **η/B law on Fashion-MNIST** | 1.05 [0.87, 1.38] and 0.94 [0.72, 1.10] | One of the six minima is capped at all three settings. The other five give 1.03 [0.97, 1.11] and 0.89 [0.86, 0.93], so the second interval excludes 1. The paper now says the law holds \"to within about 10%\", and also gives the six-minima values. |\n| **Weibull AIC gaps** | 2.1 and 0.1, called \"small\" | Those figures cover all 36 conditions. On the 28 used for H1, gamma beats Weibull by 5.1 and lognormal by 6.4, so I dropped \"small\". Weibull beats shifted exponential by 6.9, not 4.9. |\n| **Doubling η** | 9.4× | Kept, but two capped minima enter it; without them it is 8.5×. |\n| **Adam comparison** | Narrow 2.75×, wide 1.89× | Kept, and added values using only minima with observed medians: 2.01× narrow and 1.91× wide (n=3 each). This supports \"no width dependence\". The ablation table also gets observed-only values, 0.50 and 0.41. |\n| **Small corrections** | k = 1.19, ratio 0.94, saddle \\|λ₁\\| of 1e-4 to 1e-3 | k = 1.18, ratio 0.93, \\|λ₁\\| of 2e-4 to 0.03 |\n\nThe new Fashion-MNIST η/B intervals come from my own bootstrap over five minima, and the observed-only Adam and ablation values are my own geometric means. They are not in `results/analysis/summary.json`, so someone repeating that analysis won't find them there. `paper_draft/OUTLINE.md` lists every change above.\n\n**Citations:** titles and authors for the arXiv papers match arXiv metadata. Venues and years in `references.bib` come from what I know of the published versions, not from an online check. Ibayashi & Imaizumi and Jastrzębski et al. are cited as arXiv preprints because I couldn't confirm a venue. I added Kingma & Ba for Adam and Alpaydin & Kaynak for the digits dataset.\n\n**Additions to the requested setup:**\n- `\\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}`, needed for the Polish author names in the bibliography.\n- The `\\@trackname` fix that `[final]` requires.\n- `enumitem`, `algorithm` and `algpseudocode`.\n- An appendix with the preregistered criteria and deviations.\n\nThere is no method figure; `algorithm 1`, the exit check, takes that role in the introduction. `paper_examples/` holds only a README, so the style comes from the lab guide and `templates/paper_writing/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1059,"cache_read_input_tokens":160753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1059},"output_tokens":865,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f205d79e-9dcc-4336-8ac8-c0edce33ebd6","uuid":"037c9e11-ed64-46ad-8d8c-bf418aebaaa5","timestamp":"2026-10-31T07:02:09.038Z","request_id":"req_011CgZtKs7ujC8wrfEysp7do"}
